WEBVTT

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.980
Oh, you survived?

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.360
That's quite a greeting, out of the blue.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.740
Have you heard the rumors?

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.490
I'm being treated as something of a hero right now.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.770
I haven't. Why are you here?

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.790
I received a summons from House Eris.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.280
I called him here.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:30.970
Brother.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:34.720
This is the first time we have seen one another, is it not, Sion Astal?

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.580
I am the head of House Eris, Lucile Eris.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.070
I called you here today for one simple reason.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:50.980
I wish to hear of your feelings.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.480
My feelings?

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.790
I will now ask you many questions.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:00.150
They will be used to determine whether or not you are suitable.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.920
I would like for you to answer them.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.760
However, I do have one condition before you undergo questioning.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:11.270
If I don't like any one of your answers, I will kill you.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.340
Calm yourself. You will not feel a thing.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.300
You will not even notice your head being detached from your body.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.600
Your expression tells me you that you do not understand.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.930
But this is the House of Eris, Sion Astal.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.540
I see.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.920
The master of the house, which has served generations of kings, wishes to test me?

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:42.700
All the descendants of this kingdom's founder, Aslude Roland, have that right.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.210
Even the son of a low-born cur.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.890
Very well. I'll play along. Ask what you will, Lucile Eris.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:55.230
I thought you would. Come with me.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:01.850
What a waste. Would you throw away that life,
which you kept with such difficulty on the battlefield, here?

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.020
My hard-earned survival gives me all the more reason to do this.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.550
Out of the way, out of the way!

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.890
The Duke is coming through!

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.600
Can you come home earlier today?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:16.500
No, a new prisoner came in. It'll take a while to get him settled.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.520
Oh, I see. I don't know what he did, but how pitiful.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:24.730
Yeah, once you go in there, you'll never see the sun again.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.960
The next time he goes outside, it'll probably be to his...

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.460
Is he still young?

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.930
Yeah, not even twenty.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.380
Old man! Hey, old man prison guard!

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.260
What is it today?

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.730
So, what do you want today?

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.970
Hmm... paper and a pencil.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:57.110
Oh! Also, you know the Royal Special Military Academy?

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:00.580
There are some books at their library that I'd like to borrow.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:05.750
Books, huh? Well, that sounds reasonable enough.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:09.630
Really?! I want thirty in total, though.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.940
Th-Thirty?!

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:26.390
Making a web here? You sure about that?

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:30.100
This cell doesn't even let flies in.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.720
Tough as always... C'mon!

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.650
Here, I'll share some.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:50.570
I brought 'em.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:53.780
Oh! Thanks, old man!

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.520
What are you doing, gathering so many books day after day?

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.980
Sorry, but could I ask you to get me another ten books?

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.520
What? You still don't have enough?!

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.700
What, you still awake?

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.480
Hm? Yeah.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.410
You're an odd one.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:32.820
Normally, being stuck in this dark atmosphere would really get to somebody.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:36.800
Even the noisiest guys go quiet after a week or so.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.480
Most can't handle a month...

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.140
You're a <i>real</i> odd one.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.960
Hey, here's today's delivery.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.380
Oh, thank you.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:03.100
After the Royal Special Academy comes the Aslude Memorial Library, huh?

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.200
You sure you're not trying to gather books from every library in the country here?

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.040
Is your daughter over her cold?

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.250
Yeah, she's doing great!

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:17.690
Oh, listen to this! She finally stood up and walked by herself!

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:20.110
Really? That's great!

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:24.880
Seeing my own child grow this much is so moving!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.070
These kids grow up before you even know it!

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.390
Come on, she just started walking.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:34.760
If you get like this now, what'll you be like when she grows up and gets married?

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.470
I won't allow that!

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:41.380
Hey, don't tell me you're after my daughter? Is that it?!

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.570
What made you jump to that conclusion? Calm down!

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.200
You've got to hang in there.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:52.370
Well, when your daughter grows up,

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.040
you'd hate to see her go to war or anything, wouldn't you?

00:07:56.040 --> 00:08:00.860
Of course! What world has parents that want to send their children to war?

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:02.680
Yeah, I guess so.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.100
War really does suck.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:19.360
Old man! Something smells really nice today, doesn't it?

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:23.150
You noticed? I went for a little luxury today.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.860
A hot garlic chicken and cheese sandwich!

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:29.520
And here I have to live with sour soup every day!

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.260
My wife's business has been doing great lately.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:34.570
You really do have to have your meat!

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.320
You two work together, don't you?

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.210
Yeah, I help her sell vegetables at the morning market.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:45.240
There's still the baby to consider,
so I don't like her working so hard.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.290
Still, I'd take that any day over being a soldier.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.130
There was a huge war seven years ago.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.180
I was in the army back then.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:56.890
We were deployed to the battlefield,
and everyone, including my friends, died.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.970
I thought all the time about how much I hated war.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:01.820
That's true, isn't it?

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:06.500
That's why I turned down an officer position and came here.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.800
It's a tough life, but I have no regrets.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.450
Is that right?

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:21.540
Wee! Look how tall you are!

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.600
I see.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.230
So, this is the path you've chosen.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:54.700
If you think you can keep taking afternoon naps here forever, you're dead wrong.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:19.890
You're really curious, aren't you?

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:24.970
There are plenty of places that are brighter and easier to live in, with better food.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.780
Why are you so fixated on this place?

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:46.520
That was bad. I thought I was going to suffocate.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:49.700
If I don't clean this place up, I'll die.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.530
Well, I'll just have breakfast for now.

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:54.780
After another nap, I'll take my time...

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:01.340
Hey, old man, I've been waiting. What's for breakfast...?

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.530
What's wrong, old man?

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.240
Did something happen?

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.910
Did you have another fight with the wife?

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:17.150
Or did you get depressed when your daughter introduced a boyfriend?

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:20.850
Don't be ridiculous! My daughter is still three years old!

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:23.090
Three-year-olds these days are something else.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:24.510
Haven't you heard, old man?

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:28.510
Something else? What do you mean? My daughter isn't like that!

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.350
That's what every parent says.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:32.040
You're wrong!

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:36.020
You're wrong. That's not it...

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.620
What's really the matter? Hey, where's my breakfast?

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:50.610
I see. It's okay, you don't have to tell me.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.310
That's what this is about, right?

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.390
The date of my execution been decided.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:59.470
This country's finally grown too scared of keeping a monster locked away.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:05.290
Well, I guess I should be grateful that they let me live close to two years.

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:08.340
Oh, right, old man.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.520
Could you help me carry the research report I've been writing here?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:17.070
My orders said not to allow you to take anything with you...

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:23.230
Oh, I see. well, I guess someone scheduled to die doesn't need this stuff.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.220
Don't make such a long face, old man. Let's go.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:39.830
See you. Take care.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.920
Ryner, where are you going?

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:58.200
Ryner, bye bye!

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.030
Is this Ryner Lute?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.150
Well, then, I'm off. Thanks for everything.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:42.900
Hey, hottie.

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:44.760
What is it, sex fiend?

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.620
Well, uhm... What's with that?

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.350
Would you mind if I asked why you called me a sex fiend?

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.560
It's your face.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:01.990
And your personal history. I've heard all about you.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:07.030
Oh, well. Sorry, but I'm going to make a break for it.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.980
Oh, you think you can take me?

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.980
I once made a promise.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:14.320
I can't afford to die yet.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:17.420
What I seek is thunder... Izuchi!

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.070
A-Are you kidding me?

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:35.730
Aw, man... I might get killed if I don't take this seriously.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.690
Oh? You weren't serious just now?

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:42.110
Well, I'd say about 70% serious.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.570
I see. That's why he wants you.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:47.920
Let's go!

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.090
Hold on, time out!

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:52.370
I offer up this contract to bear the wicked spirit beast which sleeps in the earth!

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:15.700
You've got to be kidding me! What magic are you using to keep up with mine?

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.800
None? Nothing?

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:25.300
She's doing all this without even using magic? That's ridiculous!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.720
What I seek is the water cloud... Mizui!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.800
You were holding back just now.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:50.430
What makes you say that?

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:55.680
If you had used flame magic with a wider area of attack just now, instead of water magic,

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.350
it should have been possible for you to catch me.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.860
But if I did that, you could have died, right?

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.950
I'd hate to burn such a pretty face.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:11.490
I see. My beauty, great enough to destroy the world,

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:15.790
filled your sex-crazed head with wild fantasies on the battlefield

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:18.000
and prevented you from making rational decisions.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.210
So that's how it went.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:22.240
Destroy the world...?

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.980
Come, let's go. The King awaits.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:29.180
Hey. Where would you find a guy that'd walk willingly to his execution?

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:34.350
Stay behind if you'd rather. But you'll severely regret it later.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.710
Oh, for crying out loud!

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:54.870
What's happened to this country?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.210
Welcome, Ryner, to my royal court.

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:03.280
Yo.

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:10.300
I'm beat today. I'm taking a nap.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.350
Good night.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.910
Hey, you're still in the King's presence!

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.680
Who cares? I'm tired!

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.370
So, how was he?

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.290
A sex fiend, just as I expected.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:25.900
If you leave him as he is, he'll likely commit a horrifying crime within a few years.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:27.150
And?

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:31.690
He's the first person to go easy on me, aside from my brother.

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:32.990
Is that right?

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:38.380
Knock it off, Ryner. I won't tell you about Kiefer.

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:40.740
I don't care.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.130
She's dead.

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:45.900
I'm kidding.

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:47.540
You little...

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:51.700
Kiefer left the country, and asked me to look after you.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.550
She said she wanted to go out and see more of the world.

00:17:56.430 --> 00:18:00.420
But I didn't have you brought here today to tell you that.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.100
My report?

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.820
"How to Build a Kingdom of Afternoon Naps."

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:09.170
A silly title, but the contents are rather fascinating.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.910
Relics of the legendary heroes...

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:16.490
using their incredible power as a deterrent to eliminate wars across the world.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.330
Amazing. You've really thought this through.

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:21.950
Don't read others' reports without asking.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:24.350
I've taken a shine to this report.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:30.830
As such, Ryner, I would like for you to travel all over the world

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.540
and gather these hero relics and whatnot, starting now.

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:35.720
What?! Why me?!

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:39.260
But I'm worried that you'd slack off by yourself.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.740
Ferris, I would like for you to accompany him as an assistant.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.810
For the sake of world peace, let me ask this one thing of you.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:50.440
Who'd do that?! I just wrote that report as a way to pass the time!

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.570
If you don't obey my orders, you'll get the death penalty.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:55.660
What's peaceful about this?!

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.480
You bastard, what are you thinking?

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:00.730
I am merely assisting you on my brother's orders.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.540
I am not your henchman.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:06.500
I've received Lucile's permission. In his words...

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:12.870
"If Ferris disobeys, the Wynnit dumpling shop will be crushed on the spot"... it seems.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.940
You have two minutes to begin your journey.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:19.360
What was that voice just now?

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:21.210
He's serious.

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:25.080
We have no time. Let's get going, sex fiend.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:27.710
I said we have no time. Choose.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:30.520
One: lose your head. Two: lose your torso.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:33.150
Three: do as I say. What will it be?

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:36.330
Damn you, Sion! You'll regret this!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.690
You finally feel like going?

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.410
Who would?!

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:40.670
One minute left.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:44.110
Anyhow, will someone tell me who that voice is?!

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.200
Well then, I'm off, King.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.330
Take care of Ryner.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:51.870
Don't proceed with anything without getting permission!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.310
Let's go, partner.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.050
Who are you calling partner?!

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:02.980
Lucile, is this the place I'm headed?

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:09.470
It's one possibility of the future.
This place isn't your ultimate goal.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:14.850
That's why I haven't killed you yet.
A king is an object. One cog in a kingdom.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.440
It won't break when it's new.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.610
You're still new.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.780
<i>I'll walk my own path.</i>

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:27.720
<i>Ryner, is this the path you chose?</i>

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:32.260
<i>It's a good one, though it's different from mine.</i>

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:38.550
<i>People hate dying. They hate killing, too.</i>

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:41.740
<i>They don't like making others cry, or crying themselves.</i>

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:45.970
<i>How must it feel to not be able to choose one's life?</i>

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:50.330
<i>What about when family dies? Or when a loved one dies?</i>

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:53.870
<i>Nobody wants those things.</i>

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:59.180
<i>Yet, the world laughs and hungers for such suffering.</i>

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:03.760
<i>I've never had a burning desire to change something.</i>

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:06.890
<i>But it would be sad to live without change.</i>

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:09.310
<i>I don't want to lose anything else...</i>

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:15.010
<i>It's a pain, but I think it's about time we moved forward.</i>

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:18.210
<i>I've averted my eyes until now, but...</i>

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.090
<i>If I have to, I'll take a hard look at my own past,</i>

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:26.520
<i>to achieve a world where nobody ever loses anything.</i>

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:29.740
<i>One that doesn't make that child or Kiefer cry.</i>

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.420
<i>One where Tahile, Tony, and Fahle don't die.</i>

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:35.060
<i>One where Sion doesn't have to brood.</i>

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:39.040
<i>A world where everyone can laugh...</i>

00:21:39.350 --> 00:21:43.410
<i>...and take afternoon naps all the time.</i>

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>Ugh, this is seriously a pain!</i>

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.010
<i>This is more of a bother than I thought possible!</i>

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:30.760
<i>And what's with this troublesome woman being my partner?</i>

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:33.260
<i>Hey, wait, no violence...!</i>
